maya: Heads-up: onboarding sample-app ran into a subtle embed + rerank ordering bug during partial retries. We batch 4 inputs, one chunk partially fails, helper retries the lone item and then concatenates by arrival order, which breaks the expected [id-order] pairing for rerank.

sam: Oof, do you have the log dump and which helper + sdk version? Node or Python?

maya: Node sample-app, embed-helper v0.9.2. Logs show initial send:

```json
{"batch":"batch-7","items":[{"id":"u1","text":"foo"},{"id":"u2","text":"bar"},{"id":"u3","text":"baz"},{"id":"u4","text":"qux"}]}
```

Chunker sent two chunks of 2. Chunk 1 succeeds, chunk 2 times out on second item (u4). Helper then retries u4 solo. Responses come back in this order: resp(chunk1 items), resp(retry u4), resp(chunk2 item u3) — because of async timing. Helper just pushes into result array as responses arrive. Final vector array maps to [u1,u2,u4,u3] while rerank code assumes positions map to original ids.

todd: That's definitely a reassembly bug. Helpers must either preserve original indices or return an envelope of {id, embedding}.

sasha: Note: our Python helper already preserves an index map for partial retries (added in PR #214). Node helper never received that parity PR. We should align them.

maya: Current embed-helper.js (simplified):

```js
async function embedAll(items){
  const chunks = split(items, 2);
  const results = [];
  await Promise.all(chunks.map(async c => {
    try{
      const r = await client.embeddings.create({input: c.map(i=>i.text)});
      results.push(...r.data);
    }catch(e){
      // retry naive
      for(const it of c){
        const rr = await client.embeddings.create({input:[it.text]});
        results.push(rr.data[0]);
      }
    }
  }));
  return results; // broken when concurrency + retries reorder
}
```

maya: The quick fix: allocate an output array of length items.length, and write each returned embedding into its original slot based on index. If we don't get index back from server, the helper must track mapping before sending.

sam: I'll send a PR to: 1) include item._orig_idx when constructing requests, 2) on response map returned vectors to _orig_idx, and 3) make a feature flag to request server to echo ids in responses (embeddings.create({input, echo_ids:true})).

todd: Also add unit tests that simulate network races: send chunks, randomly delay responses, ensure final ordering equals input ordering. Add integration test that wires rerank flow to verify consistency.

sasha: One more edge: some customers expect embedding responses to be array-only for speed, others want {id, vector}. We should document both and offer helper-level conversion. Also the SDK should provide a stable helper that guarantees order instead of leaving it to apps.

maya: Agreed. I can patch sample-app to use the new mapping helper and update onboarding guide to call out "helpers guarantee input-order, do not rely on server echo unless you opt-in".

ci-bot: ci/test-embed-helper: new tests added for index-preserving merge (flaky simulation)  triggered by @sam branch.

sam: Will follow up with a Node/Python parity PR and docs blurb in devex repo. Thanks for catching this — would have been noisy in prod rerank jobs.

maya: Thanks all. Leaving a note in the sample-app README and a link in the onboarding checklist. :rocket:
